{
  "title": "Ingredient parser: cover the citrus juiced/zested lines citrus.rs still skips",
  "description": "ingredient_parser/citrus.rs reads \"1 lemon, juiced\" / \"2 limes (zested and juiced)\" as lemon juice / lime zest, but some fixture lines still fall through to the generic parser: \
\"1 large grapefruit (juiced)\" and \"2 large grapefruits, juiced (about 2 cups)\" (parse_prep_tail only takes lemon/lime/orange because bespoke.json has no per-grapefruit juice yield; add one, then widen the list), \
\"1 blood orange, juiced\" (FRUIT_REGEX has no blood orange; the catalog may need a blood orange juice mapping too), \
\"1 lemon, juiced and zest freshly grated\" (mixed participle + noun phrase), \
\"1 lemon (zested for topping)\" (a word follows the phrase, which the parser refuses to guess at), \
\"3 medium clementines (zested and fruit inside blended)\", and \
\"1 lemon (juiced, about 1/4 cup fresh lemon juice)\" / \"1 lemon, juiced ((approx. 2 TBSP lemon juice))\", where the volume ends up in the note instead of leading the measurements because the trailing \"lemon juice\" words stop parse_ingredient from reading it. \
Each of these gives a whole-fruit or unmatched item today. Expect small data/ diffs from make pipeline.",
